  "id": "COMPOUND:18839 - PROTEIN:5787",
  "verbalization": "Plakortide N is implicated in the biological pathway leading to RXF 631 through multiple indirect mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Plakortide N acts as a target for several compounds, which in turn target RXF 631. Specifically, Plakortide N is linked to Malme-3M, a compound that is a target of Opposit-4(15)-Ene-1Beta,11-Diol and 2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid, both of which have RXF 631 as their target. This indicates that Plakortide N may influence RXF 631 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving the activation of downstream signaling pathways. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, albeit indirect, relationship between Plakortide N and RXF 631, likely mediated by the compounds that act as intermediaries in the pathway. The integration of these evidence points highlights a potential role for Plakortide N in modulating RXF 631 activity through a complex network of molecular targets.",
